% review-findings: A Maratha lullaby to the infant Rama as Vishnu ("It was Vishnu's self that was born on the lap of Kaushalya"), with devas strewing flowers: Hindu devotional words.
% review-suggestion: Keep; label it a devotional lullaby, as above.
% review-decision: published to main on 11 November 2026 labelled a devotional lullaby (N: schools follow their own guidance on religious songs), with bars 4 and 5 rebarred to make two whole 3/4 bars ("born" shortened from a quarter to an eighth, the barline moved one beat later so the rest and "Little" end bar 5) and the final rest dropped; bars 4 to 6 and the refrain's second bar still to be checked against the plate; keep correcting here
